WEBVTT

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:12.450
Teacher, this is amazing.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.750
We are now in Castle Carbunculus.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:21.670
Her Majesty The Queen
is somewhere within these walls!

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.010
I call this my office,
but it's rather like my hobby room.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.550
Make yourselves at home.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.970
Is something the matter?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.140
No, forgive me.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.940
This morning, Domi couldn't
believe I knew nothing about you.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.400
Oh, you need not worry about that.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.780
It makes sense, considering you
are the Shapeless One's child.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.910
And truth be told,

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:58.250
your teacher genuinely loathes me.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:03.380
He even disliked my name passing his lips.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.380
I have no doubt he'd eradicate all traces
of my name to keep it from your eyes.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:13.840
That... sounds like something he might do.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.640
Yes, it does, doesn't it?

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:21.600
That machine interests you?

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.440
It's a difference engine
given to me by Marquis Machina.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.280
And that is a lamp powered by astermite.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:28.650
Over there is--

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.110
Lord Ruthven.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.860
Sorry to interrupt the fun,

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.570
but can we cut to the chase?

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:47.500
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.260
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.640
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.230
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:09.480
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:16.990
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:25.580
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:34.550
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:39.430
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:44.100
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.690
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.440
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:02.290
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.750
Noé, Vanitas.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:12.130
First, I would like to
thank you for your heroic actions.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.300
Lucius has told me everything.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:21.810
Thanks to you, our brethren's casualties
at the ball were kept to a minimum.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:25.560
What are your thoughts
on the attack that day?

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.230
It was Charlatan.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:33.110
I'd thought they were hallucinations
that only curse-bearers could see.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:39.450
But now, I believe that attack
was an attempt on Lucius's life.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.120
I agree.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.000
The chaos caused by the curse-bearers

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.710
was likely an attempt to
distract the Queen's Fangs.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:55.130
If that black shadow, Naenia,
is the one that steals true names,

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:59.300
it's no surprise there were
a number of curse-bearers there.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.890
Um, by Lucius, you mean Luca?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.770
Why would they try to kill him?

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:08.890
What? You still don't get it?

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.110
The boy has rank and power
second only to the queen.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:17.400
No doubt, there are countless nobles
who feel he's in their way.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.280
Isn't that right, Luca?

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.990
Or should I say, Lucius,
Grand Duke Oriflamme.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.700
Grand duke? Really?!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.960
The grand duke is
Her Majesty's close advisor.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:30.790
That's right.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.750
That is amazing!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.590
I would not call it amazing.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:41.840
Lord Uncle, who is also my guardian,
handles all of my duties as grand duke.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:46.810
In any case, my succession to
the office hasn't been made official.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.350
My blood ran cold
when I heard you ventured

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.810
into the mortal world without leave.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:59.030
You must be more conscious
of your own position.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.570
Yes, Lord Uncle.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:03.450
Come to think of it, Luca,

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:08.450
weren't you seeking <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>
to save your brother?

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.960
My big brother suffers dearly from
the Vampire of the Blue Moon's curse!

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:16.040
Where is he now?

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.420
Let us forget about that.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:24.550
Huh?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:29.140
I'm telling you not to mention
the boy's brother ever again.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.150
Salvation takes many forms.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:42.990
Freeing him from the curse is not
necessarily in his best interest.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:46.870
But enough about that.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:51.750
You're here to ask me
about curse-bearers, aren't you?

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:57.500
I, too, have many questions I would
ask you of the Blue Moon Clan.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:00.130
Questions about the
Vampire of the Blue Moon,

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:03.880
<i>The Book of Vanitas</i>, and...

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:07.140
...about you yourself.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.060
You're right.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:16.350
We should devote this time
to more fruitful discussions.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:21.230
Which is why I'd like to
start with my request.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:24.150
What is it? Speak.

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.740
I thought you'd never ask.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.200
Take me to your queen.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.540
What?

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.210
Did you not hear me?

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.000
I'm telling you to take me to your queen.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.130
To what purpose?

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:43.670
My purpose? It's simple.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:49.930
I believe it is the queen
that gives rise to curse-bearers.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.020
Don't spout such nonsense, human!

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.180
What's the big deal?

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.140
Just let me see her.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:07:00.190
I merely wish to examine every nook
and cranny of Her Majesty's body.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:01.110
Insolent fool!

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.690
Well, Ruthven? What say you?

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:08.030
It should be easy with
the grand duke's prerogative.

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:13.540
How long has it been since
the queen was seen in public?

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:17.540
Why has she become a hermit?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:19.380
Vanitas.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.710
I ask you...

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:21.130
Uncle?

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:24.460
...does your queen yet live?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.490
Lord Uncle?

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:48.280
Please, stop.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.780
Lord Uncle!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:53.120
Leave this place at once, human.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:59.170
Every word you have spoken maligns
the good name of our queen!

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:04.920
I forbid you from ever
setting foot in this castle again!

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.760
So they booted us back across the barrier.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:12.720
It's been about a week since
we got back to the human world.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.270
Every bone in my body aches,
so I've been sleeping it off.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:19.520
They sent Murr back later.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.400
That's all we have to report!

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:26.820
Blasted fools!

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.240
You dare show such
insolence toward the queen?!

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:29.990
Count Orlok!

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.450
Please calm yourself!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:32.320
Wanna fight?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.330
--I'll rip you to shreds!
--Think you can take me?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.330
It worked out fine.

00:08:35.330 --> 00:08:40.080
I got the information that I most wanted.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:49.010
He played us for fools.

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:52.140
That human wasn't interested in me.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:54.680
It was you, Lucius.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:09:00.190
Most vampires fly into a blind rage
when Her Majesty is insulted.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.400
You should have, too.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.860
But you...

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:11.450
You showed a moment of dismay.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.530
That was the same as confirming his words.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:23.330
Your Majesty...

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:26.960
What am I to do?

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.720
So, until the dust settles,

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.300
I will keep curing curse-bearers
as I've been doing.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.390
But I need information--

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:37.310
Impudent, human!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:40.640
Master Orlok has no time for you!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:43.900
Another incident?

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:46.610
"Vampires disappear."

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:49.570
"Three in one week." That's a lot.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:50.820
Hands off the files!

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:52.950
Get the hell out!

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.870
Hey, quack.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:00.410
Oh, Dante, perfect timing.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.710
Wait. What happened?

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.000
Leave it!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.920
I've got some new info on curse-bearers.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.670
I'll do you a solid and sell it to you!

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.260
It was yesterday

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:19.810
that we finally located this curse-bearer
who slipped into Paris not long ago.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.560
That's when...

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:27.980
She was abducted right before our eyes.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.820
But like an idiot, Riche tried to stop it.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.070
I got dragged in and beat up, too.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.610
I never asked you to save me.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.320
What did you say, hag?

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.660
Shut it, fatty!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:39.080
Hag!

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:39.580
Fatty!

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:41.910
All right, children, no need to fight.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:42.500
Butt out!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.040
Fatty!

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:46.460
Johann, you got pretty beat up, too!

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.460
What is your problem?!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.710
When I was all alone,

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:52.460
I was mistaken for a vampire
and nearly abducted.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:56.260
But they fled the moment
they realized I was a dham.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.090
That was so rude.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.100
A dham?

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:02.720
Mixed race. You know,
half-vampire, half-human?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.230
All three of us are.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:09.310
You've never seen a dhampir before?

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.150
No.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:12.190
Hey, quack.

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:15.740
A little trophy I tore off
the abductor's coat.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:19.410
A sword and six wings?

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.040
Vani...

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:28.630
I know who abducted the vampires
and who old-man Orlok's after.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:32.920
It's the Church's anti-vampire unit,
the Chasseurs.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.220
Captain, have you heard?

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:37.260
It's about that human.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.890
Of course, I have.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:41.350
Vanitas, was it?

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:44.680
Not only was he made
minion of the Blue Moon Clan,

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:50.360
but they say vampires are flocking to
his side in an attempt to use his power.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.980
What a...

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.610
What a...!

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.150
Poor, pitiful child!

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:04.620
We must do whatever it takes to
save him in the name of the Lord!

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:15.420
The Catacombs of Paris.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:20.720
Once an old stone quarry, they were
later converted into a vast ossuary.

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:28.020
"Halt. The Empire of the Dead lies ahead."

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:29.520
I'm shocked.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:33.400
I knew there was an ossuary beneath Paris,

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:37.400
but now it's a tourist attraction?

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:38.780
How can I put it?

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.530
It's such a curious place.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:44.030
It is, but the ossuary
is only a teeny part

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:47.040
of the tunnel network beneath Paris.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.290
Vanitas.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.090
Dante saw the Chasseurs heading down here,

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:58.130
but do you really think we'll
find them in this labyrinth?

00:12:58.130 --> 00:12:59.510
Beats me.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:02.430
But I often heard that
the Chasseurs wiped out

00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:05.720
the vampires infesting
the tunnels under wartime Paris

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:10.350
and then established a base down here,
or so the story goes.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:15.320
Based on that, Dante must've
come down here to find a way there.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:18.650
Wouldn't it be better to
seek help from Count Orlok

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.950
in investigating the disappearances?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.070
Oh, I think not. That would be impossible.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:29.290
The bad blood between the vampires
and Chasseurs still runs deep.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:32.250
One false move and you guessed it.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:35.790
Another war could break out.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.880
In short, the count
must watch his every step.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:42.220
Precisely.

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:46.930
Like I said, Dante, I wish you
wouldn't make matters worse.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:47.810
Stop yapping!

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:50.930
I won't rest till I pay 'em back
for that beat down!

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.480
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:53.940
Stop that!

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.440
The devil take them!

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.400
Where'd those robed bastards get to?!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.610
Enough already.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:03.660
That tourist trap can't
possibly provide any clues.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:07.660
It was beyond stupid to look
for their base through the catacombs.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.540
What?!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:12.370
Unexpected clues sometimes turn up
where you least expect them!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:12.580
--Idiot, idiot, idiot!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:16.460
--Baldy, baldy, baldy!
--Idiot, idiot, idiot!

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.550
What's this? Worried
about Vanitas, are we?

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:21.130
I suppose so.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:24.010
He's acting perfectly normal.

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:25.970
So I wonder.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:29.720
Why would he be acting so?

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:11.560
What took so long?

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:14.640
I almost finished this book.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:18.360
I don't know where
we're going, but fear not.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:20.400
I took a respectable catnap.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.320
Couldn't care less!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:26.530
Off to investigate
the disappearances, I take it?

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.240
None of your business.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:31.620
So you really do think
the Chasseurs are behind this?

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:33.120
Stop following me.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.960
I'm not following you.

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:40.840
I'm joining you.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.010
Suit yourself.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:48.760
Yes, I'll do that.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.730
Noé, this way.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:04.190
Wait. Vanitas!

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.740
Hey! What are you doing there!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.240
Perfect timing.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:17.620
All right! These disguises
should get us in.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.290
Shall we?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:26.630
Um... It should be around here.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:34.260
Where does that lead?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.390
The catacombs.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.470
The catacombs?

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:39.100
Not the same ones from earlier today.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:44.230
We're going where only
those in the know can travel.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:50.530
The Chasseurs' secret lair.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:17:00.460
How do you know about this place?

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.500
It's as if you've been here before.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.090
Never a hesitant step.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.760
Vanitas!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:14.510
Please tell me.
You already know, don't you?

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:19.350
Who really abducted those vampires?

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:24.690
Chasseurs who aren't
really Chasseurs at all.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:29.190
What does that mean?

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.490
Listen, Noé.

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:33.620
If we encounter Chasseurs,
and it comes to a fight,

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:37.040
they will go straight for your eyes.

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:40.870
Underestimate human adversaries,
and you'll end up dead.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:57.470
This place looks different from
the catacombs we saw earlier today.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.890
Are these the remains of those
who were somehow special?

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.390
No. This is--

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:06.110
All the bones you see here
are from vampires!

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:14.160
Look at this one. It still has its fangs.

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:17.870
Vestiges of formulaic alteration even
in death are a sign that this was

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:21.000
a high-ranking vampire.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.790
All the bones in this chamber

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:27.420
are from vampires our predecessors
slew in the underground labyrinth.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:30.300
The slayer's name is
carved above each one.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:35.470
They vied to behead the most vampires
and be deemed the mightiest.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.180
Um, and you are?

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.350
Who am I?

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:43.440
My name is Roland Fortis.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:47.020
I am the Sixth Paladin,
graced with the Jasper Gem.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.230
A paladin?

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:52.280
You're one of the twelve captains
of the Chasseurs!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:54.150
Stop. You're making me blush.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:57.820
I didn't make captain until recently.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.660
My posting to this
district was recent, too.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:06.210
I was on a patrol-slash-walk
to drill the map into my head.

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.000
So, who are you?

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.050
What are you doing here at such an hour?

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.170
We beg your forgiveness!

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:16.340
I am Vincent, and this is Gilbert.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:20.010
We discovered a secret
passage in the church.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:25.020
We should have reported it at once,
but we ventured in to investigate.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.900
We ended up getting
lost for several hours.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:29.860
So you're lost?

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:32.070
Same as me.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:33.320
Huh?

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:37.950
H-Hold on. Sir Roland,
are you saying that you're lost?

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.450
Yes, that's right.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:43.200
I'm at a total loss.
I can't find my way back.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:48.380
But the Lord's hand is in all things.

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:53.760
How else could I have come
across you after losing my way?

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.760
Now, follow me!

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.300
Have no fear.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:03.640
My trusty subordinates are
bound to be searching for me.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:13.110
Noé, it could get ugly if he takes
us back to the Chasseurs' guard post.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:15.820
Is there some way to silence him?

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:20.240
No. At least none that I can see.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.210
All this was beneath our feet?

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:31.710
What's this?

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.670
Vincent, Vincent!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:36.260
Could you come here a moment?

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:37.220
Sir?

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.590
This writing on the wall...

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:40.970
Writing?

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.600
Aw, hell!

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:49.190
Noé, close your eyes!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.860
A flash grenade?

00:20:57.780 --> 00:21:01.240
What is this? My vision is...

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:10.120
I thought so. You're a vampire.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.630
Do you suffer?

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:18.300
That light you just beheld has the
power to render your eyes useless.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:25.970
The real world and the
formulaic world are blurring together.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.770
Noé!

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:35.360
That clothing does not belong to you.

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:40.200
Did you slay those you stole it from?

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.070
N-No...

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:45.240
I don't know why you're here.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:51.790
But no vampire who sets foot
in here leaves this place alive.

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:54.210
We are the Chasseurs.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:58.210
Those who corrupt the
divine law of God's creation,

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:01.300
the crimson-eyed heretics, are our prey!

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:04.390
We are the Lord's eternal blade!

00:22:04.390 --> 00:22:06.720
Amen!

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:12.100
Where Death Slumbers

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:47.110
Those Who Hunt Crimson
